Changes grouped by release:

11-06-26 Release
================
* ImpCre no longer loops forever (printing "I don't know what you mean"
  millions of times a second) when its input ends at the "create the data
  files?" question, e.g. when run from a script. It now creates nothing,
  says why, and exits with status 1; set DoNotAsk=1 to create the files
  without being asked
* Combat: planets can now have weapons and use them.
  - "install 12p <item>" / "remove 12p <item>" put blasers and photon
    torpedo tubes into a planet's 8 weapon slots
  - "fire <target> 12p" fires from a planet. Blasers are powered by ore,
    torpedoes use missiles and planet mobility; planets need the same
    military/officers as a ship to fire, and aim with their own tech
    level and efficiency
  - Defensive fire: an attacked planet fires back at full strength, and
    the defender's (and allies') armed planets in range help, as ships
    set to defend already did. Planet attackers get torpedoes back
  - Planet weapons are damaged when the planet is hit, and recover while
    installed. Installed weapons can't be loaded or sold
  - New "doc combat"; fire/install/remove help updated
* Fix planet shelling reducing the counts of big items on a planet without
  touching the items themselves; big items on a planet are now damaged
  one by one (also when planes crash onto it)
* Fix a blaser miss leaving the target ship locked
* Fix torpedoes aimed at a planet reading garbage for the "target in a gas
  cloud" check
* Fix defensive fire treating the ship with the same number as an attacked
  planet as the target (it fired back at full strength)
* Fix the weapon chart showing efficiency/TF figures that were too low
* Fix "remove" of an engine never recalculating the ship's engine stats
* Deity: fix "edit updates" refusing resDecreaser/techDecreaser values that
  ImpCre itself sets, and "edit player" refusing every Credits value on
  64-bit systems
* load/unload help gave the big item and ship in the wrong order
* systemd services: "make install-systemd" installs imperium.service,
  imperium-telnet.service and an optional daily imperium-publish.timer,
  all running as impown with sandboxing. "make install-user" creates
  the impown account
* Fix telnet players who hang up without "bye" staying marked as logged
  on (TelImp was killed by SIGPIPE before it could log them out).
  Stopping TelImp now logs every connected player out properly
* ImpServ removes a server port left behind by a crash instead of
  refusing to start
* The nostart file is found in the installed data directory (was always
  /usr/local/lib/imperium/data) and its message is printed
* Build: autoconf/configure removed - Linux only now. Just "make" and
  "make install". One Makefile with automatic header dependencies,
  parallel builds (make -j), DESTDIR support, and a clear message if the
  install user/group does not exist. Changing IMP_DEST rebuilds
  automatically. config.h is now a normal source file
* All sprintf/strcpy/strcat replaced with bounded versions; a compile
  time check makes sure every buffer size really is an array size
* Client pipes are created atomically (no more tempnam); the external
  editor temp file uses mkstemp
* Install: fifo/ is now sticky (1777) so users can't delete or replace
  each other's pipes, and fifo/server is writable only by the game
  owner so nobody can pose as the server. Existing ic.allow/is.allow
  are no longer overwritten
* Fix ImpCre storing the Secret setting in the port field, and
  default.sh/bigworld.sh not passing Name, Host, Port and Secret on
* Fix "discharge" crashing (divide by zero) when the planets have
  nobody on them, and negative numbers being accepted by load/teleport
  and similar commands
* Fix time handling for 32-bit systems with a 64-bit time_t (e.g.
  current Raspberry Pi OS)
* Database IS compatible with 1.5 - no data file changes
* Builds on current Linux (tested Ubuntu 24.04 / GCC 13, and with the
  stricter error checks that GCC 14 turns on by default)
* "make" no longer hangs when there is no terminal (scripts, Docker, CI).
  Set IMP_CON_CODE, IMP_CTRL_CODE and IMP_SHUT_CODE to choose the secret
  codes, or random ones are generated
* Fix server security check randomly failing on modern crypt libraries
  (salt was not NUL terminated) - this broke ImpShut
* Fix ImpShut crash on 64-bit systems (cuserid)
* Fix TelImp: did not compile, failed to start when the hostname did not
  resolve, and dropped players with "got bad val from select()"
* Fix help/doc file requests being able to read files outside the help
  and doc directories
* Email is sent without going through the shell, and no longer crashes
  if the temp file can't be created
* Fix plague code notifying a non-existent player for unowned planets
* Fix new player email prompt returning garbage when cancelled
* Library and ImpCre now get the configured CFLAGS
* Many buffer overflow fixes (sprintf -> snprintf)

